/* =============================================================================
   Bacteriology MIC — Phase 1 (per "MIC Document" protocol images).
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Adds a Method selector (Disk Diffusion / MIC) to each Enteric Pathogen row's
   AST panel. When the user picks MIC, the existing Disk Diffusion antibiotic
   grid is hidden and this file's panel is shown instead: same 14-antibiotic
   list, same per-row Interpretation pill, but zone inputs become free-text MIC
   inputs validated by bdsis_mic_normalize_value() (grammar already used by
   E. coli AST MIC entries).

   Phase 1 scope — ship this session:
     * Method dropdown + DD/MIC toggle (lab.php)
     * MIC panel renderer + hardcoded breakpoints (this file)
     * iu-lab.php reads method[rowIdx] and routes save
   Phase 2 — deferred:
     * Salmonella/Shigella/Enterococcus pathogen-specific antibiotic subsets
     * β-lactam resistance "new variable after Pathogen 3" MIC columns
     * Admin seeding of ms_ast_table method='02' rows (replaces hardcoded map)

   Breakpoints match image 2 of the MIC Document. The symbolic values below
   (e.g. "≤8", "16^", "≥32", "2/38") are what the panel RENDERS as reference
   hints. For live interpretation we use the numeric 's' / 'r' thresholds
   extracted alongside them (clean floats), compared against the first numeric
   substring of whatever the user types.

   Database:
     Reuses bacteriology_ast_table -- the schema already has `ast_method_id`
     (VARCHAR) and `zone_diameter` (VARCHAR(10) wide enough for MIC strings
     like "<=0.5", "0.12-0.5^"). No ALTER needed. `ast_result` holds the
     interpretation. ast_method_id is '01' for Disk Diffusion rows (unchanged)
     and '02' for MIC rows added by this file.
   ============================================================================= */

